<!--Post: 6096--><!--Time: 1107532312-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6096"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Surfietx<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Surfietx<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 7:51 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->After thinking about drop #8, I thought that perhaps the sign itself was more important than the drop.  I noticed that there was an arrowhead turning left.  I then cross-referenced to the T. Bob Kreisch post about going down arrowhead street and turning left on Iroquois.  I googled Iroqois and found that the tribe originates in New York.  That then brought me to Kevin Bright&#39;s statements.  Anyway, the research took this interesting path. <BR> <BR>First: <BR> <BR><a href="http://homepage.mac.com/thorntonstreiff/The_Wichita_Group.html#The%20Fantastic%20Fifties:%20Part%20I" target=_top>http://homepage.mac.com/thorntonstreiff/The_Wichit a_Group.html#The%20Fantastic%20Fifties:%20Part%20I</a>   <BR> <BR>Click on the &#34;Fantastic Fifties, part 1 <BR> <BR>Then: <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.geocities.com/bakfan_uk/Bruce_Conner.htm" target=_top>http://www.geocities.com/bakfan_uk/Bruce_Conner.ht m</a> <BR> <BR>Then: <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.canyoncinema.com/C/Conner.html" target=_top>http://www.canyoncinema.com/C/Conner.html</a> <BR> <BR>Then: <BR> <BR><a href="http://archivesofamericanart.si.edu/oralhist/conner73.htm" target=_top>http://archivesofamericanart.si.edu/oralhist/conne r73.htm</a> <BR> <BR>It&#39;s a lot to read, but interesting nonetheless. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6096-->
<!--Post: 6108--><!--Time: 1107535093-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6108"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lorenap<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lorenap<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 8:38 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->verrrrrrrrry interesting!  <BR>He&#39;s exactly the type of person I see btk being. A real oddball! It sounds like this guy spent much of his time in California though. Zodiak?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6108-->
<!--Post: 6115--><!--Time: 1107537297-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6115"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Surfietx<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Surfietx<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 9:14 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Notoriously illusive, he&#39;s periodically dropped out of sight throughout his career, and his productivity came to a complete halt four years ago when he contracted a rare liver disease. <BR> <BR>Conner the man is hardly what you&#39;d expect in light of his work.  Meeting with him at his exceptionally orderly house, one encounters a neat, soft-spoken gent who obviously quenches his thirst for chaos and grunge in his work. <BR> <BR>&#34;I&#39;ve descended into this private hell of being an artist who&#39;s thought of as dead, but, in fact, I&#39;m still living,&#34; he says with a laugh.  <BR> <BR>That&#39;s from this link:  <a href="http://www.geocities.com/bakfan_uk/Bruce_Conner.htm" target=_top>http://www.geocities.com/bakfan_uk/Bruce_Conner.ht m</a> <BR> <BR>The Dillons connection and the university connection are also really, really eerie, and there is so much more. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6115-->
<!--Post: 6159--><!--Time: 1107555784-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6159"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 2:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Why is the Dillons connection eerie?  I don&#39;t know that the Dillons are anything but a very nice, albeit wealthy, family.   <BR> <BR>Is there supposed to be some connection between BTK and the Dillons?  Because I have not heard of one to this point.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6159-->
<!--Post: 6161--><!--Time: 1107556489-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6161"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Surfietx<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Surfietx<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 2:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Isn&#39;t that where the Otero&#39;s car was left/found...Dillons parking lot?  I found it weird because his father was a manager at Dillons, that&#39;s all.  No offense to the family themselves. <BR> <BR>Did you read the links I provided en toto prior to asking your question?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6161-->
<!--Post: 6317--><!--Time: 1107676821-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6317"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Kansasgirl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Kansasgirl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 06, 2005 - 12:00 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->GET A SWAB! That gave me the chills reading the story. He said his films were based on sex, death and violence. I wonder what a timeline would look like with the murders and his location? Any unsolved murders in other areas where he lived? His picture was that of a well dressed man who probably carried a briefcase and fits into society. Very strange!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6317-->
<!--Post: 6567--><!--Time: 1107894969-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6567"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Wilmac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wilmac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 12:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The only problem is that he&#39;s lived in San Francisco since the 1960&#39;s...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6567-->
<!--Post: 6569--><!--Time: 1107896134-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6569"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Surfietx<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Surfietx<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 12:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Wilmac, why is that a problem?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6569-->
<!--Post: 6576--><!--Time: 1107898560-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6576"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Newyorker<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Newyorker<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 1:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The murders were in Kansas during the 70s &amp; 80s ... <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6576-->
<!--Post: 6586--><!--Time: 1107902645-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6586"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Wilmac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wilmac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 2:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well, for one, they don&#39;t get KAKE in San Francisco. How would he know Susan Peters had a cold unless he was watching every night?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6586-->
<!--Post: 6676--><!--Time: 1107957440-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6676"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Surfietx<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Surfietx<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 5:57 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->How do we know he is in San Fran right now?   <BR> <BR>For the sake of the argument:  My parents have a couple of homes scattered throughout the U.S.  They use one as their primary address, but travel and vacation to the other locations during the year.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6676-->
